rinciple: Tunica externa (adventitia) is principally collagenous and elastic connective tissue and supports the vessel in surrounding tissues.","E":"The listed choice is not supported by the key principle: Tunica externa (adventitia) is principally collagenous and elastic connective tissue and supports the vessel in surrounding tissues."},"references":[{"title":"OpenStax — Structure and Function of Blood Vessels","url":"https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/20-1-structure-and-function-of-blood-vessels"}],"review":"reference_reviewed_duplicate_identical_question_and_options","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","questionTextHash":"ca4d9819ac9ef905eecb206ba39b5173600ba8a759c29034d1aecb2a31b8e406","provisional":false},"q-2dff6e2cfd61":{"correct":"A","answerText":"cytoplasm between ribosomes, tRNA and mRNA","explanation":"Translation takes place on cytoplasmic ribosomes, with mRNA providing the template and tRNA delivering amino acids. Transcription, by contrast, makes RNA from DNA.","optionReasons":{"A":"Translation takes place on cytoplasmic ribosomes, with mRNA providing the template and tRNA delivering amino acids. Transcription, by contrast, makes RNA from DNA.","B":"nucleus between ribosomes, tRNA and mRNA — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Translation takes place on cytoplasmic ribosomes, with mRNA providing the template and tRNA delivering amino acids. Transcription, by contrast, makes RNA from DNA.","C":"nucleus between DNA and mRNA — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Translation takes place on cytoplasmic ribosomes, with mRNA providing the template and tRNA delivering amino acids. Transcription, by contrast, makes RNA from DNA.","D":"cytoplasm between DNA and mRNA — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Translation takes place on cytoplasmic ribosomes, with mRNA providing the template and tRNA delivering amino acids. Transcription, by contrast, makes RNA from DNA."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"f57f960575b63721a987470a7169d955d9f2abaed73bde17b6d7d845fa20a30d"},"q-28f134143b82":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Capillary","explanation":"Gas and solute exchange occurs chiefly across capillary walls because they consist of a very thin endothelial barrier and offer enormous total surface area.","optionReasons":{"A":"Gas and solute exchange occurs chiefly across capillary walls because they consist of a very thin endothelial barrier and offer enormous total surface area.","B":"Arteriole — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Gas and solute exchange occurs chiefly across capillary walls because they consist of a very thin endothelial barrier and offer enormous total surface area.","C":"Venule — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Gas and solute exchange occurs chiefly across capillary walls because they consist of a very thin endothelial barrier and offer enormous total surface area.","D":"Elastic artery — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Gas and solute exchange occurs chiefly across capillary walls because they consist of a very thin endothelial barrier and offer enormous total surface area.","E":"Muscular artery — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Gas and solute exchange occurs chiefly across capillary walls because they consist of a very thin endothelial barrier and offer enormous total surface area."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"b35f82ce1ae4f7dac874f0fdb885dbbb5c15e65af58f47140dbb7b6806e24aaf"},"q-10d8322935e1":{"correct":"C","answerText":"The posterior interosseous nerve pierces supinator.","explanation":"The deep branch of the radial nerve passes through the supinator muscle and continues as the posterior interosseous nerve. The common extensor origin is lateral, not medial.","optionReasons":{"A":"Brachioradialis is innervated by the posterior interosseous nerve. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The deep branch of the radial nerve passes through the supinator muscle and continues as the posterior interosseous nerve. The common extensor origin is lateral, not medial.","B":"The common extensor origin is the medial epi- condyle of the humerus. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The deep branch of the radial nerve passes through the supinator muscle and continues as the posterior interosseous nerve. The common extensor origin is lateral, not medial.","C":"The deep branch of the radial nerve passes through the supinator muscle and continues as the posterior interosseous nerve. The common extensor origin is lateral, not medial.","D":"The extensor retinaculum is attached to the radius and the ulna. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The deep branch of the radial nerve passes through the supinator muscle and continues as the posterior interosseous nerve. The common extensor origin is lateral, not medial.","E":"The extensor tendons pass through the extensor retinaculum in the same fascial compartment. 4 — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The deep branch of the radial nerve passes through the supinator muscle and continues as the posterior interosseous nerve. The common extensor origin is lateral, not medial."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"8f6c0e595a788a2a9e9c7e01e8536ffefafb87fba7425c35cbca9ba643398b69"},"q-dc0f1a22e9e3":{"correct":"C","answerText":"In early stage may present with a dry cough and asthmatic wheezing.","explanation":"Hookworm larvae penetrate skin, migrate through the lungs and may produce cough or wheeze before reaching the intestine. Diagnosis typically uses stool eggs rather than perianal tape.","optionReasons":{"A":"Is usually spread by the faeco-oral route — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Hookworm larvae penetrate skin, migrate through the lungs and may produce cough or wheeze before reaching the intestine. Diagnosis typically uses stool eggs rather than perianal tape.","B":"May block the pancreatic duct causing pancreatitis — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Hookworm larvae penetrate skin, migrate through the lungs and may produce cough or wheeze before reaching the intestine. Diagnosis typically uses stool eggs rather than perianal tape.","C":"Hookworm larvae penetrate skin, migrate through the lungs and may produce cough or wheeze before reaching the intestine. Diagnosis typically uses stool eggs rather than perianal tape.","D":"Eggs can be readily distinguished microscopically from those of Strongyloides sp. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Hookworm larvae penetrate skin, migrate through the lungs and may produce cough or wheeze before reaching the intestine. Diagnosis typically uses stool eggs rather than perianal tape.","E":"It is diagnosed by microscopy of adhesive tape prints taken from the perianal area — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Hookworm larvae penetrate skin, migrate through the lungs and may produce cough or wheeze before reaching the intestine. Diagnosis typically uses stool eggs rather than perianal tape."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"0373b34b3203487f9ab008c75c11ee82710eb8f7d323d9fff9bf1e0f070e8ef6"},"q-6f1d4a8feaaf":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Halothane","explanation":"Halothane has a recognized association with rare severe immune-mediated hepatotoxicity and hepatic necrosis; the other listed inhalation agents have much lower risk of that syndrome.","optionReasons":{"A":"Soveflurane — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Halothane has a recognized association with rare severe immune-mediated hepatotoxicity and hepatic necrosis; the other listed inhalation agents have much lower risk of that syndrome.","B":"Desflurane — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Halothane has a recognized association with rare severe immune-mediated hepatotoxicity and hepatic necrosis; the other listed inhalation agents have much lower risk of that syndrome.","C":"Halothane has a recognized association with rare severe immune-mediated hepatotoxicity and hepatic necrosis; the other listed inhalation agents have much lower risk of that syndrome.","D":"Nitrous oxide — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Halothane has a recognized association with rare severe immune-mediated hepatotoxicity and hepatic necrosis; the other listed inhalation agents have much lower risk of that syndrome."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"a228f99d9c6a034ba2158e5734391054cdc95adaf6e9eb451d29b2f7f31d6a0b"},"q-78660938d1f8":{"correct":"A","answerText":"REM sleep","explanation":"Rapid-eye-movement sleep is particularly associated with vivid narrative dreams and physiological muscle atonia; dreaming can also occur in non-REM sleep.","optionReasons":{"A":"Rapid-eye-movement sleep is particularly associated with vivid narrative dreams and physiological muscle atonia; dreaming can also occur in non-REM sleep.","B":"Slow wave sleep — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Rapid-eye-movement sleep is particularly associated with vivid narrative dreams and physiological muscle atonia; dreaming can also occur in non-REM sleep.","C":"Stage 2NR