k conduction of sensory impulses, usually by inhibiting voltage-gated sodium channels, without necessarily altering consciousness.","D":"A stupor or somnolent state — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Local anesthetics block conduction of sensory impulses, usually by inhibiting voltage-gated sodium channels, without necessarily altering consciousness."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"d8ffc0aa6e28d918216e82684a50dba60c767a10a187f9c68e02291c0421c4fa"},"q-4ce6aaeac0bd":{"correct":"B","answerText":"The study of how the body works.","explanation":"Physiology is the study of how living organisms and their parts function. Histology describes microscopic tissues, and homeostasis is one physiological process.","optionReasons":{"A":"The microscopic study of tissues and cells — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Physiology is the study of how living organisms and their parts function. Histology describes microscopic tissues, and homeostasis is one physiological process.","B":"Physiology is the study of how living organisms and their parts function. Histology describes microscopic tissues, and homeostasis is one physiological process.","C":"All the chemical processes that take place in the organelles of the body’s cells. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Physiology is the study of how living organisms and their parts function. Histology describes microscopic tissues, and homeostasis is one physiological process.","D":"The body’s automatic tendency to maintain a relatively constant internal environment. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Physiology is the study of how living organisms and their parts function. Histology describes microscopic tissues, and homeostasis is one physiological process."},"references":[],"review":"independent