ifies a patient's reported and observed abnormal mental experiences without requiring a causal explanation.","D":"Philosophical psychiatry — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Descriptive psychopathology documents and classifies a patient's reported and observed abnormal mental experiences without requiring a causal explanation.","E":"None of the above — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Descriptive psychopathology documents and classifies a patient's reported and observed abnormal mental experiences without requiring a causal explanation."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"b387e03ac1dc5dcc469c9f0a82e1f9abfa4c6b540e71ebfab176490a01717746"},"q-b07c67640dc2":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Prilocaine","explanation":"Prilocaine can cause methemoglobinemia through its metabolite o-toluidine, which oxidizes hemoglobin iron from ferrous to ferric form.","optionReasons":{"A":"Prilocaine can cause methemoglobinemia through its metabolite o-toluidine, which oxidizes hemoglobin iron from ferrous to ferric form.","B":"Procaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Prilocaine can cause methemoglobinemia through its metabolite o-toluidine, which oxidizes hemoglobin iron from ferrous to ferric form.","C":"Lidocaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Prilocaine can cause methemoglobinemia through its metabolite o-toluidine, which oxidizes hemoglobin iron from ferrous to ferric form.","D":"Ropivacaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Prilocaine can cause methemoglobinemia through its metabolite o-toluidine, which oxidizes hemoglobin iron from ferrous to ferric form."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHas