 vena cava.","D":"The right bundle branch has anterior and pos- QUESTIONS terior divisions. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The atrioventricular node lies in the inferior interatrial septum near the coronary sinus opening. The sinoatrial node is by the superior vena cava, not inferior vena cava.","E":"The sinoatrial node is supplied by the right coro- nary artery in 40% of cases. THORAX: — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The atrioventricular node lies in the inferior interatrial septum near the coronary sinus opening. The sinoatrial node is by the superior vena cava, not inferior vena cava."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"7fbb45ef6ad359c9d93a0a54571159f6f642c4ff97d1b27fd0828a7d24261c40"},"q-d9e610d177fe":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Formoterol","explanation":"Formoterol is a beta-2 adrenergic agonist used for bronchodilation in asthma, generally in an inhaled corticosteroid-containing regimen.","optionReasons":{"A":"Formoterol is a beta-2 adrenergic agonist used for bronchodilation in asthma, generally in an inhaled corticosteroid-containing regimen.","B":"Norepinephrine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Formoterol is a beta-2 adrenergic agonist used for bronchodilation in asthma, generally in an inhaled corticosteroid-containing regimen.","C":"Methoxamine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Formoterol is a beta-2 adrenergic agonist used for bronchodilation in asthma, generally in an inhaled corticosteroid-containing regimen.","D":"Dobutamine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Formoterol is a beta-2 adrenergic agonist used for bronchodilation in asthma, generally in an inhaled corticosteroid-containing regimen."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no