stion. Distinguishing fact: Chordae tendineae tether atrioventricular valve leaflets to papillary muscles, preventing leaflet prolapse into the atria during ventricular systole.","C":"Closure of the aortic valve is best heard in the left 2nd intercostal space. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Chordae tendineae tether atrioventricular valve leaflets to papillary muscles, preventing leaflet prolapse into the atria during ventricular systole.","D":"The chorda tendinae tether the atrioventricular valves to pectinate muscle directly. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Chordae tendineae tether atrioventricular valve leaflets to papillary muscles, preventing leaflet prolapse into the atria during ventricular systole.","E":"Chordae tendineae tether atrioventricular valve leaflets to papillary muscles, preventing leaflet prolapse into the atria during ventricular systole."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"6df44beb141072ec3e0c7bd1cf91912763593afe02b12c15dd7f6f993e1baab8"},"q-ffce69a6fc84":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Lilliputian hallucination","explanation":"Miniature people or animals perceived in a hallucination are termed lilliputian hallucinations and may occur during withdrawal states or delirium.","optionReasons":{"A":"Micropsia — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Miniature people or animals perceived in a hallucination are termed lilliputian hallucinations and may occur during withdrawal states or delirium.","B":"Macropsia — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Miniature people or animals perceived in a hallucination are termed lilliputian hallucinations and may occur during withdrawal states or delirium.","C":"Miniature people or animals perceived in a hallucination are termed lilliputian hallucinations and may occur during w