e size. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Simple columnar epithelium comprises one layer of tall epithelial cells; 'simple' means one cell layer and 'columnar' denotes tall cell shape.","C":"several layers of cells, all of the same type. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Simple columnar epithelium comprises one layer of tall epithelial cells; 'simple' means one cell layer and 'columnar' denotes tall cell shape.","D":"several layers of cells but without a basement membrane. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Simple columnar epithelium comprises one layer of tall epithelial cells; 'simple' means one cell layer and 'columnar' denotes tall cell shape."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"c125ad4fc38a1f7cb6e6da8adaa009e9fa773ec2c73bca3e04c004f83f780374"},"q-0246e1d5e81d":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Procaine","explanation":"Procaine is a relatively short-acting ester local anesthetic compared with bupivacaine, ropivacaine and commonly lidocaine.","optionReasons":{"A":"Lidocaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Procaine is a relatively short-acting ester local anesthetic compared with bupivacaine, ropivacaine and commonly lidocaine.","B":"Procaine is a relatively short-acting ester local anesthetic compared with bupivacaine, ropivacaine and commonly lidocaine.","C":"Bupivacaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Procaine is a relatively short-acting ester local anesthetic compared with bupivacaine, ropivacaine and commonly lidocaine.","D":"Ropivacaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Procaine is a relatively short-acting ester local anesthetic compared with bupivacaine, ropivacaine and commonly lidocaine."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_bat