ns.","B":"Triazolam — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Clorazepate forms the long-lived active metabolite desmethyldiazepam, increasing next-day residual sedation compared with shorter-acting options.","C":"Clorazepate forms the long-lived active metabolite desmethyldiazepam, increasing next-day residual sedation compared with shorter-acting options.","D":"Lorazepam — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Clorazepate forms the long-lived active metabolite desmethyldiazepam, increasing next-day residual sedation compared with shorter-acting options."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"78542b1e43e7964ed9c716a8fc155668b267a45e7bc4c7c3f0b2d791e0cd08b2"},"q-c6aaa84f1f21":{"correct":"C","answerText":"The coronary sinus lies in the posterior interven- tricular groove.","explanation":"The coronary sinus runs in the posterior atrioventricular (coronary) sulcus, not the posterior interventricular groove. The other named veins ordinarily drain as described.","optionReasons":{"A":"Venae cordis minimae drain into all four chambers. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The coronary sinus runs in the posterior atrioventricular (coronary) sulcus, not the posterior interventricular groove. The other named veins ordinarily drain as described.","B":"The anterior cardiac veins drain into the rightQUESTIONS atrium. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The coronary sinus runs in the posterior atrioventricular (coronary) sulcus, not the posterior interventricular groove. The other named veins ordinarily drain as described.","C":"The coronary sinus runs in the posterior atrioventricular (coronary) sulcus, not the posterior interventricular groove. The other named veins ordinarily drain as described.","D":"The middle cardiac vein is a tributary of the cor-