t the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: J chains participate in polymerization of IgM pentamers and dimeric IgA; their loss disrupts these polymeric immunoglobulin forms.","D":"IgG and IgM — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: J chains participate in polymerization of IgM pentamers and dimeric IgA; their loss disrupts these polymeric immunoglobulin forms.","E":"J chains participate in polymerization of IgM pentamers and dimeric IgA; their loss disrupts these polymeric immunoglobulin forms."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"f97ff96a4b51f000292622e8b86c8590d44768e09c3711e3f7aa949a48dc68f6"},"q-3863a1611e2d":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Leptospira interrogans","explanation":"Leptospirosis is caused by Leptospira species and can present after farming or animal-water exposure with fever, headache and photophobia or conjunctival suffusion.","optionReasons":{"A":"Treponema pallidum — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Leptospirosis is caused by Leptospira species and can present after farming or animal-water exposure with fever, headache and photophobia or conjunctival suffusion.","B":"Leptospirosis is caused by Leptospira species and can present after farming or animal-water exposure with fever, headache and photophobia or conjunctival suffusion.","C":"Borrelia burgdorferi — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Leptospirosis is caused by Leptospira species and can present after farming or animal-water exposure with fever, headache and photophobia or conjunctival suffusion.","D":"Borrelia recurrentis 44 – Mycoplasma and Ureaplasma — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Leptospirosis is caused by Leptospira species and can present after farming or animal-water exposure with fever, headache and photophobia or conjunctival suffusion."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"cc381ce89a768cd6187608bc52f194237a984c5c2dfdac346d2cde8205365048"},"q-55bc0150d8ce":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Gradual occlusion at its bifurcation leads to claudication in the lower limb.","explanation":"Chronic aortoiliac occlusive disease around the abdominal aortic bifurcation can cause lower-limb and buttock claudication, classically termed Leriche syndrome.","optionReasons":{"A":"It enters the abdomen at the level of the 1st lumber vertebra, — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Chronic aortoiliac occlusive disease around the abdominal aortic bifurcation can cause lower-limb and buttock claudication, classically termed Leriche syndrome.","B":"Azygos vein lies on its left side. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Chronic aortoiliac occlusive disease around the abdominal aortic bifurcation can cause lower-limb and buttock claudication, classically termed Leriche syndrome.","C":"It ends at the level of 5th lumber vertebra, — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Chronic aortoiliac occlusive disease around the abdominal aortic bifurcation can cause lower-limb and buttock claudication, classically termed Leriche syndrome.","D":"It is crossed anteriorly by the head of the pancreas. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Chronic aortoiliac occlusive disease around the abdominal aortic bifurcation can cause lower-limb and buttock claudication, classically termed Leriche syndrome.","E":"Chronic aortoiliac occlusive disease around the abdominal aortic bifurcation can cause lower-limb and buttock claudication, classically termed Leriche syndrome."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"9d7b47f8f442d8a08c4cdc2b66077a130df52080a02624440a7915bf0b48e488"},"q-885be2fa8599":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Recall bias","explanation":"Case-control studies often compare retrospective exposure histories between cases and controls, making them susceptible to recall bias if recollection differs by disease status.","optionReasons":{"A":"Blinding of an independent observer — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Case-control studies often compare retrospective exposure histories between cases and controls, making them susceptible to recall bias if recollection differs by disease status.","B":"Blinding of the investigator — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Case-control studies often compare retrospective exposure histories between cases and controls, making them susceptible to recall bias if recollection differs by disease status.","C":"Complies with Helsinki agreement on ethics — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Case-control studies often compare retrospective exposure histories between cases and controls, making them susceptible to recall bias if recollection differs by disease status.","D":"Case-control studies often compare retrospective exposure histories between cases and controls, making them susceptible to recall bias if recollection differs by disease status."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"9a1b8fa8d87b7b2b549592586de9e483cf76090393e3bb1af030884b401b498d"},"q-86a7b0fd78a0":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Cytotoxic or anticancer drugs given to the mother are safe during pregnancy.","explanation":"Cytotoxic chemotherapy during pregnancy may injure embryonic or fetal tissues and is not generally considered safe; timing and specific agents determine the risk.","optionReasons":{"A":"Gross anatomical defects in the fetus are unlikely to result from drugs in late pregnancy. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Cytotoxic chemotherapy during pregnancy may injure embryonic or fetal tissues and is not generally considered safe; timing and specific agents determine the risk.","B":"Sex hormones, when taken during pregnancy, may harm the fetus. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Cytotoxic chemotherapy during pregnancy may injure embryonic or fetal tissues and is not generally considered safe; timing and specific agents determine the risk.","C":"A vasoconstrictor drug may cause fetal distress. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Cytotoxic chemotherapy during pregnancy may injure embryonic or fetal tissues and is not generally considered safe; timing and specific agents determine the risk.","D":"Cytotoxic chemotherapy during pregnancy may injure embryonic or fetal tissues and is not generally considered safe; timing and specific agents determine the risk.","E":"Teratogenic drugs may produce harmful effect, especially if given in early pregnancy. | P a g e ٨ General Pharmacology MCQs — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Cytotoxic chemotherapy during pregnancy may injure embryonic or fetal tissues and is not generally considered safe; timing and specific agents determine the risk."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"124a681e0c862aeb4284678a024ae51b44f8d36c30898285af0f220e01e885d9"},"q-deefffac9e7a":{"correct":"D","answerText":"blood","explanation":"Blood is a specialized connective tissue because its cells are suspended in a fluid extracellular matrix (plasma).","optionReasons":{"A":"pancreas — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Blood is a specialized connective tissue because its cells are suspended in a fluid extracellular matrix (plasma).","B":"spinal cord — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Blood is a specialized connective tissue because its cells are suspended in a fluid extracellular matrix (plasma).","C":"muscle — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Blood is a specialized connective tissue because its cells are suspended in a fluid extracellular matrix (plasma).","D":"Blood is a specialized connective tissue because its cells are suspended in a fluid extracellular matrix (plasma)."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"863f70d2b7e154328a14c6a4be5a2fc6b2db60f54e490fb5d2f40fd1a91c0c42"},"q-cc408be41f79":{"correct":"B","answerText":"body conditions relatively constant within a narrow range through negative and positive feedback.","explanation":"Homeostasis maintains internal conditions within a regulated physiological range rather than enforcing exact unchanging values.","optionReasons":{"A":"a constant internal body environment through negative feedback. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Homeostasis maintains internal conditions within a regulated physiological range rather than enforcing exact unchanging values.","B":"Homeostasis maintains internal conditions within a regulated physiological range rather than enforcing exact unchanging values.","C":"adequate concentrations of respiratory gases. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Homeostasis maintains internal conditions within a regulated physiological range rather than enforcing exact unchanging values.","D":"blood glucose level within the healthy range. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Homeostasis maintains internal conditions within a regulated physiological range rather than enforcing exact unchanging values."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"3750e0194ce1f2c19c9d423dd8e732d33c88aef25626b33979628122d85599a2"},"q-7cd8492f2243":{"correct":"C","answerText":"formation of defective collagen fibres.","explanation":"Vitamin C is required for proline and lysine hydroxylation during collagen synthesis; deficiency produces poorly stabilized, structurally defective collagen.","optionReasons":{"A":"a decreased number of collagen fibres. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Vitamin C is required for proline and lysine hydroxylation during collagen synthesis; deficiency produces poorly stabilized, structurally defective collagen.","B":"an increased elastin:collagen ratio. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Vitamin C is required for proline and lysine hydroxylation during collagen synthesis; deficiency produces poorly stabilized, structurally defective collagen.","C":"Vitamin C is required for proline and lysine hydroxylation during collagen synthesis; deficiency produces poorly stabilized, structurally defective collagen.","D":"detachment of ribosomes in fibroblasts. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Vitamin C is required for proline and lysine hydroxylation during collagen synthesis; deficiency produces poorly stabilized, structurally defective collagen.","E":"insufficient ground substance. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Vitamin C is required for proline and lysine hydroxylation during collagen synthesis; deficiency produces poorly stabilized, structurally defective collagen."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"dfb16902f99d3e5a76f1e1f6116f888914bfaed0c8f8575ec54aa5ac8e597741"},"q-3dc38c4e4093":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Rickettsia rickettsii","explanation":"Rocky Mountain spotted fever is caused by Rickettsia rickettsii, classically associated with tick exposure and fever, headache and a spreading rash.","optionReasons":{"A":"Orientia tsutsugamushi — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Rocky Mountain spotted fever is caused by Rickettsia rickettsii, classically associated with tick exposure and fever, headache and a spreading rash.","B":"Coxiella burnetii — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Rocky Mountain spotted fever is caused by Rickettsia rickettsii, classically associated with tick exposure and fever, headache and a spreading rash.","C":"Rocky Mountain spotted fever is caused by Rickettsia rickettsii, classically associated with tick exposure and fever, headache and a spreading rash.","D":"Rickettsia prowazekii — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Rocky Mountain spotted fever is caused by Rickettsia rickettsii, classically associated with tick exposure and fever, headache and a spreading rash."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"2544e0606251faf76cee7972b22901975112756c9d328e89348e8edf49eaf85f"},"q-2cd456dc6da5":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Drug biotransformation in the organism","explanation":"Pharmacokinetics includes drug absorption, distribution, metabolism (biotransformation) and elimination, not the drug's effects on target tissues.","optionReasons":{"A":"Complications of drug therapy — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Pharmacokinetics includes drug absorption, distribution, metabolism (biotransformation) and elimination, not the drug's effects on target tissues.","B":"Pharmacokinetics includes drug absorption, distribution, metabolism (biotransformation) and elimination, not the drug's effects on target tissues.","C":"Influence of drugs on metabolism processes — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Pharmacokinetics includes drug absorption, distribution, metabolism (biotransformation) and elimination, not the drug's effects on target tissues.","D":"Influence of drugs on genes — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Pharmacokinetics includes drug absorption, distribution, metabolism (biotransformation) and elimination, not the drug's effects on target tissues."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"ecf08e59900d88b5e0c43c990d16b3a74bbf026257e72314d5eb39dbb61491e5"},"q-7a9f08d94743":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Pericyte","explanation":"Pericytes surround capillaries and small venules and retain mesenchymal differentiation potential, contributing to vessel stabilization and repair.","optionReasons":{"A":"Fibroblast — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Pericytes surround capillaries and small venules and retain mesenchymal differentiation potential, contributing to vessel stabilization and repair.","B":"Endothelial cell — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Pericytes surround capillaries and small venules and retain mesenchymal differentiation potential, contributing to vessel stabilization and repair.","C":"Pericytes surround capillaries and small venules and retain mesenchymal differentiation potential, contributing to vessel stabilization and repair.","D":"Histiocyte — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Pericytes surround capillaries and small venules and retain mesenchymal differentiation potential, contributing to vessel stabilization and repair.","E":"Macrophage A pericyte is a pluripotential cell that is prevalent around post capillary venules. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Pericytes surround capillaries and small venules and retain mesenchymal differentiation potential, contributing to vessel stabilization and repair."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"30ae0197ec2d8f3ab841d8282285e08dae0215c091d2d73a01ce424d6d7331d6"},"q-822350b9390e":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All the ganglia receive white rami communicants.","explanation":"Lumbar sympathetic ganglia generally receive gray rami, while white rami are limited to thoracolumbar spinal levels T1 to L2; not every lumbar ganglion receives a white ramus.","optionReasons":{"A":"It enters the abdomen behind the medial arcuate ligament. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lumbar sympathetic ganglia generally receive gray rami, while white rami are limited to thoracolumbar spinal levels T1 to L2; not every lumbar ganglion receives a white ramus.","B":"The right trunk descends behind the right margin of the inferior vena cava. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lumbar sympathetic ganglia generally receive gray rami, while white rami are limited to thoracolumbar spinal levels T1 to L2; not every lumbar ganglion receives a white ramus.","C":"The left trunk descends on left side of the abdominal aorta. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lumbar sympathetic ganglia generally receive gray rami, while white rami are limited to thoracolumbar spinal levels T1 to L2; not every lumbar ganglion receives a white ramus.","D":"Lumbar sympathetic ganglia generally receive gray rami, while white rami are limited to thoracolumbar spinal levels T1 to L2; not every lumbar ganglion receives a white ramus.","E":"All the ganglia send grey rami communicants to lumber spinal nerves. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lumbar sympathetic ganglia generally receive gray rami, while white rami are limited to thoracolumbar spinal levels T1 to L2; not every lumbar ganglion receives a white ramus."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"95c6e33afd16016998d587d4075819ef60cb9d9dade1db604f4995e107874b59"},"q-361bba165fda":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Insecta","explanation":"Fleas belong to order Siphonaptera within class Insecta; they are wingless laterally flattened ectoparasites.","optionReasons":{"A":"Fleas belong to order Siphonaptera within class Insecta; they are wingless laterally flattened ectoparasites.","B":"Arachnida — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Fleas belong to order Siphonaptera within class Insecta; they are wingless laterally flattened ectoparasites.","C":"Crustacea — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Fleas belong to order Siphonaptera within class Insecta; they are wingless laterally flattened ectoparasites.","D":"Cirripedia — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Fleas belong to order Siphonaptera within class Insecta; they are wingless laterally flattened ectoparasites.","E":"none of the above — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Fleas belong to order Siphonaptera within class Insecta; they are wingless laterally flattened ectoparasites."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"23cfcafc28f472f43e076479a30246072e4f7bc287d7dc1dc531e334ca343ad7"},"q-2fadeb19ac19":{"correct":"B","answerText":"a variable","explanation":"A variable is a characteristic or quantity capable of taking different values or categories across observations.","optionReasons":{"A":"a constant — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A variable is a characteristic or quantity capable of taking different values or categories across observations.","B":"A variable is a characteristic or quantity capable of taking different values or categories across observations.","C":"a cause-and-effect relationship — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A variable is a characteristic or quantity capable of taking different values or categories across observations.","D":"a descriptive relationship — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A variable is a characteristic or quantity capable of taking different values or categories across observations."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"03fc1fe5df64e1a60db7f5c4acc162358b36894a97d5f1f950388e98fd40cd91"},"q-94c3030f4827":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Reduce hepatic gluconeogenesis and promote peripheral glucose utilization","explanation":"Metformin primarily decreases hepatic gluconeogenesis and glucose output, with additional improvements in insulin sensitivity; it does not stimulate pancreatic insulin secretion.","optionReasons":{"A":"Decrease postprandial rise of blood glucose and increase glucose uptake by peripheral cells — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Metformin primarily decreases hepatic gluconeogenesis and glucose output, with additional improvements in insulin sensitivity; it does not stimulate pancreatic insulin secretion.","B":"Metformin primarily decreases hepatic gluconeogenesis and glucose output, with additional improvements in insulin sensitivity; it does not stimulate pancreatic insulin secretion.","C":"Decrease the absorption of carbohydrates from the gastro-intestinal tract — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Metformin primarily decreases hepatic gluconeogenesis and glucose output, with additional improvements in insulin sensitivity; it does not stimulate pancreatic insulin secretion.","D":"Stimulate the release of endogenous insulin from the pancreatic β-cells — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Metformin primarily decreases hepatic gluconeogenesis and glucose output, with additional improvements in insulin sensitivity; it does not stimulate pancreatic insulin secretion.","E":"Increase insulin sensitivity in the peripheral tissues — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Metformin primarily decreases hepatic gluconeogenesis and glucose output, with additional improvements in insulin sensitivity; it does not stimulate pancreatic insulin secretion."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"c5c85c1c365e60afd1de4768df7f8134a4c023741d932e30e6b6a58401fafb0f"},"q-079deba98323":{"correct":"C","answerText":"the pH of the solution decreases very slightly","explanation":"A buffer resists sudden pH changes; adding a modest amount of acid ordinarily causes only a small decrease in pH until buffering capacity is exceeded.","optionReasons":{"A":"the solution becomes acidic — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A buffer resists sudden pH changes; adding a modest amount of acid ordinarily causes only a small decrease in pH until buffering capacity is exceeded.","B":"the pH of the solution decreases significantly — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A buffer resists sudden pH changes; adding a modest amount of acid ordinarily causes only a small decrease in pH until buffering capacity is exceeded.","C":"A buffer resists sudden pH changes; adding a modest amount of acid ordinarily causes only a small decrease in pH until buffering capacity is exceeded.","D":"the pH of the solution increases slightly — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A buffer resists sudden pH changes; adding a modest amount of acid ordinarily causes only a small decrease in pH until buffering capacity is exceeded."},"