 — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Connective tissue consists of cells within extracellular matrix made of protein fibers and ground substance; epithelial tissues have closely packed cells.","B":"its cells are closely packed and held together by protein fibres. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Connective tissue consists of cells within extracellular matrix made of protein fibers and ground substance; epithelial tissues have closely packed cells.","C":"it has a high rate of cell division and no blood supply — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Connective tissue consists of cells within extracellular matrix made of protein fibers and ground substance; epithelial tissues have closely packed cells.","D":"Connective tissue consists of cells within extracellular matrix made of protein fibers and ground substance; epithelial tissues have closely packed cells."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"977e02b97025f29ba797899682507b36b6313bfc9cec667eaea2842adbe94068"},"q-cdd87dd1f992":{"correct":"E","answerText":"All of the above.","explanation":"Placental separation may be recognized through a gush of blood, change in uterine shape, lengthening of the cord and placental descent.","optionReasons":{"A":"Bleeding. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Placental separation may be recognized through a gush of blood, change in uterine shape, lengthening of the cord and placental descent.","B":"Changes of uterine shape from discoid to globular. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Placental separation may be recognized through a gush of blood, change in uterine shape, lengthening of the cord and placental descent.","C":"Lengthening of the umbilical cord. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Placental separation may be recognized through a gush of blood, change in uterine shape, lengthening of the cord and placental descent.","D":"Presentation of the placenta at the cervical os. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Placental separation may be recognized through a gush of blood, change in uterine shape, lengthening of the cord and placental descent.","E":"Placental separation may be recognized through a gush of blood, change in uterine shape, lengthening of the cord and placental descent."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"1765e08c8646dbf8cfdcc172c847dfc6d764811077f4e154f0ada388586a5617"},"q-ae744280b6cf":{"correct":"D","answerText":"More stability and greater water solubility","explanation":"Local anesthetics are generally formulated as water-soluble salts to facilitate solution preparation and improve storage stability.","optionReasons":{"A":"Less toxicity and higher potency — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Local anesthetics are generally formulated as water-soluble salts to facilitate solution preparation and improve storage stability.","B":"Higher stability and greater lipid solubility — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Local anesthetics are generally formulated as water-soluble salts to facilitate solution preparation and improve storage stability.","C":"Less local tissue damage and more potency — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Local anesthetics are generally formulated as water-soluble salts to facilitate solution preparation and improve storage stability.","D":"Local anesthetics are generally formulated as water-soluble salts to facilitate solution preparation and improve storage stability."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026