gh regulatory mechanisms.","B":"Homeostasis is the maintenance of internal physiological variables within a relatively stable range through regulatory mechanisms.","C":"the body’s use of energy to produce chemical substances and parts for growth. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Homeostasis is the maintenance of internal physiological variables within a relatively stable range through regulatory mechanisms.","D":"any body response that opposes the stimulus that initiated the response. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Homeostasis is the maintenance of internal physiological variables within a relatively stable range through regulatory mechanisms."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"39bbfb3fd7baaa0ee857697f12d22d7c9082dc07382e4a6456c6fa7c298b76f3"},"q-7a17d869828b":{"correct":"C","answerText":"46.","explanation":"Normal human somatic cells contain 46 chromosomes arranged in 23 pairs; gametes normally contain 23 chromosomes.","optionReasons":{"A":"24. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Normal human somatic cells contain 46 chromosomes arranged in 23 pairs; gametes normally contain 23 chromosomes.","B":"44. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Normal human somatic cells contain 46 chromosomes arranged in 23 pairs; gametes normally contain 23 chromosomes.","C":"Normal human somatic cells contain 46 chromosomes arranged in 23 pairs; gametes normally contain 23 chromosomes.","D":"48. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Normal human somatic cells contain 46 chromosomes arranged in 23 pairs; gametes normally contain 23 chromosomes.","E":"23. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Normal human somatic cells contain 46 chromosomes arranged in 23 pairs; gametes normally co