ance and tumor rejection.","B":"natural killer cells can reject polyomavirus-induced tumors without help from T lymphocytes. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Nude mice lack mature thymus-dependent T lymphocytes, showing how T cells are important in immune surveillance and tumor rejection.","C":"Nude mice lack mature thymus-dependent T lymphocytes, showing how T cells are important in immune surveillance and tumor rejection.","D":"B lymphocytes play no role in rejection of polyomavirus-induced tumors. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Nude mice lack mature thymus-dependent T lymphocytes, showing how T cells are important in immune surveillance and tumor rejection."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"555e21cab72b3b76881633ce51db13ee30661adaadc737037af6ec91b7e1c89e"},"q-5c6663e457ff":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Descriptive statistics 8","explanation":"Descriptive statistics organizes and summarizes observed data using measures such as frequencies, means and variability.","optionReasons":{"A":"Inferential statistics — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Descriptive statistics organizes and summarizes observed data using measures such as frequencies, means and variability.","B":"Descriptive statistics organizes and summarizes observed data using measures such as frequencies, means and variability.","C":"None of the above — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Descriptive statistics organizes and summarizes observed data using measures such as frequencies, means and variability.","D":"All of the above — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Descriptive statistics organizes and summarizes observed data using measures such as frequencies, means and variability."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"bf8c41ac57058a20fe6cffaf9e350e7b16fcd5ee604ba634c565750744b65434"},"q-21ecdf06c52d":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Enteropathogenic E. coli (EPEC)","explanation":"Enteropathogenic Escherichia coli is a recognized cause of watery diarrhea in infants, particularly in settings with poor sanitation; ETEC more classically causes travelers' diarrhea.","optionReasons":{"A":"Enteropathogenic Escherichia coli is a recognized cause of watery diarrhea in infants, particularly in settings with poor sanitation; ETEC more classically causes travelers' diarrhea.","B":"Enterotoxigenic E. coli (ETEC) — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Enteropathogenic Escherichia coli is a recognized cause of watery diarrhea in infants, particularly in settings with poor sanitation; ETEC more classically causes travelers' diarrhea.","C":"Enterohemorrhagic E. coli (EHEC) — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Enteropathogenic Escherichia coli is a recognized cause of watery diarrhea in infants, particularly in settings with poor sanitation; ETEC more classically causes travelers' diarrhea.","D":"Enteroinvasive E. coli (EIEC) — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Enteropathogenic Escherichia coli is a recognized cause of watery diarrhea in infants, particularly in settings with poor sanitation; ETEC more classically causes travelers' diarrhea.","E":"Enteroaggregative E. coli (EAEC) — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Enteropathogenic Escherichia coli is a recognized cause of watery diarrhea in infants, particularly in settings with poor sanitation; ETEC more classically causes travelers' diarrhea."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"5af6ace59391f50bfb6d48b7a7907831e75559aa3bfed8b2e987a0c72565fa0b"},"q-74cc6868fec5":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Hypovolemic shock","explanation":"Extensive burns can cause profound plasma loss and reduced circulating volume, producing early hypovolemic burn shock.","optionReasons":{"A":"Cardiogenic shock — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Extensive burns can cause profound plasma loss and reduced circulating volume, producing early hypovolemic burn shock.","B":"Extensive burns can cause profound plasma loss and reduced circulating volume, producing early hypovolemic burn shock.","C":"Septic shock — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Extensive burns can cause profound plasma loss and reduced circulating volume, producing early hypovolemic burn shock.","D":"Neurogenic shock MONEY SEX AND DRUGS....MSD — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Extensive burns can cause profound plasma loss and reduced circulating volume, producing early hypovolemic burn shock."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"f38268fd5aa9926263e9d865372cc1bff5cbf95696b53287f72e4c17dc4f2a60"},"q-0ed9548e6b68":{"correct":"E","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"The three protective meningeal layers are dura mater, arachnoid mater and pia mater.","optionReasons":{"A":"Dura mater — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The three protective meningeal layers are dura mater, arachnoid mater and pia mater.","B":"Arachnoid — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The three protective meningeal layers are dura mater, arachnoid mater and pia mater.","C":"Pia mater — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The three protective meningeal layers are dura mater, arachnoid mater and pia mater.","D":"Both a and c — Not the best choice for the stated ques