erted to calcitriol, which acts through a nuclear receptor as a steroid-like hormone regulating calcium and phosphate metabolism."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"d859552011f42fd3540a7a195c2fc805ff2a894b5ac90d39afcdee83fb1b1240"},"q-68f63e88ad35":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Passive diffusion (lipid diffusion)","explanation":"Most lipophilic drugs cross gastrointestinal epithelial membranes by passive transcellular diffusion along concentration gradients.","optionReasons":{"A":"Active transport (carrier-mediated diffusion) — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Most lipophilic drugs cross gastrointestinal epithelial membranes by passive transcellular diffusion along concentration gradients.","B":"Filtration (aqueous diffusion) — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Most lipophilic drugs cross gastrointestinal epithelial membranes by passive transcellular diffusion along concentration gradients.","C":"Endocytosis and exocytosis — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Most lipophilic drugs cross gastrointestinal epithelial membranes by passive transcellular diffusion along concentration gradients.","D":"Most lipophilic drugs cross gastrointestinal epithelial membranes by passive transcellular diffusion along concentration gradients."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"76630841c7dbfeffd0e0ae2343f7938b9c8a4e6c3ecf71eaef8d630bddf231e9"},"q-303cd288522d":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Nerves","explanation":"Nervi vasorum are nerves supplying the walls of blood vessels and regulating vascular smooth-muscle tone.","optionReasons":{"A":"Neuropil — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Nervi vasorum are nerves supplying the walls of blood vessels and regulating vascular smooth-muscle tone.","B":"Neuroglia — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Nervi vasorum are nerves supplying the walls of blood vessels and regulating vascular smooth-muscle tone.","C":"Pigmented lesion of a vessel — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Nervi vasorum are nerves supplying the walls of blood vessels and regulating vascular smooth-muscle tone.","D":"Nervi vasorum are nerves supplying the walls of blood vessels and regulating vascular smooth-muscle tone.","E":"Blood vessels Nervi vascularis are nerves of the blood vessels. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Nervi vasorum are nerves supplying the walls of blood vessels and regulating vascular smooth-muscle tone."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"e5719778c08e794abc9597c82b6743061f0577e210b7aa61dbb89ab7d31de071"},"q-81e7b7d35699":{"correct":"B","answerText":"H2PO42− destroys base and HPO4− destroys acid","explanation":"The monohydrogen phosphate ion accepts added H+ while dihydrogen phosphate neutralizes added OH−, allowing the conjugate phosphate pair to resist pH changes.","optionReasons":{"A":"H2PO42− destroys acid and HPO4− destroys base — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The monohydrogen phosphate ion accepts added H+ while dihydrogen phosphate neutralizes added OH−, allowing the conjugate phosphate pair to resist pH changes.","B":"The monohydrogen phosphate ion accepts added H+ while dihydrogen phosphate neutralizes added OH−, allowing the conjugate phosphate pair to resist pH changes.","C":"H2PO42− is basic and HPO4− is acidic — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The monohydrogen phosphate ion accepts added H+ while dihydrogen phosphate neutralizes added OH−, allowing the conjugate phosphate pair to resist pH changes.","D":"the ratio of H2PO42− : HPO4− decreases following the addition of acid. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The monohydrogen phosphate ion accepts added H+ while dihydrogen phosphate neutralizes added OH−, allowing the conjugate phosphate pair to resist pH changes."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"08a1bfb096bfbf6280d292a9397c69dd6ab091bb64492302350dbe23206b30f8"},"q-0929504433f5":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Abstinence syndrome","explanation":"Lacrimation, yawning, gooseflesh, mydriasis, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and muscular aches are characteristic of opioid withdrawal (abstinence syndrome), not opioid overdose.","optionReasons":{"A":"Tolerance — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lacrimation, yawning, gooseflesh, mydriasis, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and muscular aches are characteristic of opioid withdrawal (abstinence syndrome), not opioid overdose.","B":"Opioid overdosage — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lacrimation, yawning, gooseflesh, mydriasis, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and muscular aches are characteristic of opioid withdrawal (abstinence syndrome), not opioid overdose.","C":"Drug interactions between opioid analgesics and sedative-hypnotics — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lacrimation, yawning, gooseflesh, mydriasis, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and muscular aches are characteristic of opioid withdrawal (abstinence syndrome), not opioid overdose.","D":"Lacrimation, yawning, gooseflesh, mydriasis, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and muscular aches are characteristic of opioid withdrawal (abstinence syndrome), not opioid overdose."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"ebc29f36df83c4e9d7bff8a9a162e8914c67dd17ce8764b58c5b20d611d73896"},"q-c9a981d7873a":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Ultraviolet light","explanation":"Ultraviolet exposure is not a standard cause of delayed wound healing compared with infection, diabetes, systemic corticosteroids or repeated movement of the wound.","optionReasons":{"A":"Infection — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Ultraviolet exposure is not a standard cause of delayed wound healing compared with infection, diabetes, systemic corticosteroids or repeated movement of the wound.","B":"Ultraviolet exposure is not a standard cause of delayed wound healing compared with infection, diabetes, systemic corticosteroids or repeated movement of the wound.","C":"Lack of immobilization — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Ultraviolet exposure is not a standard cause of delayed wound healing compared with infection, diabetes, systemic corticosteroids or repeated movement of the wound.","D":"Diabetes mellitus — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Ultraviolet exposure is not a standard cause of delayed wound healing compared with infection, diabetes, systemic corticosteroids or repeated movement of the wound.","E":"Exogenous corticosteroids — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Ultraviolet exposure is not a standard cause of delayed wound healing compared with infection, diabetes, systemic corticosteroids or repeated movement of the wound."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"e2aedc18e6d39be3ef8ed45a7f681083db229fd931fe377fee613cdc1b6c1227"},"q-f58fb58e6982":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Goodpasture disease (antiglomerular basement membrane)","explanation":"Goodpasture disease involves anti-glomerular basement membrane antibodies that can cause pulmonary alveolar bleeding with rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis.","optionReasons":{"A":"Metastatic renal cell carcinoma to the lungs — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Goodpasture disease involves anti-glomerular basement membrane antibodies that can cause pulmonary alveolar bleeding with rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis.","B":"Acute tuberculosis of the kidneys and lungs — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Goodpasture disease involves anti-glomerular basement membrane antibodies that can cause pulmonary alveolar bleeding with rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis.","C":"Systemic lupus erythematosus — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Goodpasture disease involves anti-glomerular basement membrane antibodies that can cause pulmonary alveolar bleeding with rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis.","D":"Goodpasture disease involves anti-glomerular basement membrane antibodies that can cause pulmonary alveolar bleeding with rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"027f882e4fb37b0ce26f66f9794f2541dad8a5915b1ffddcbb8bd29e4776ea4c"},"q-0aa1963d4ca4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"They are recognized by helper T cells, which then activate cytotoxic T cells to kill the donor cells.","explanation":"Donor HLA class II molecules are recognized by recipient CD4 helper T lymphocytes and drive cellular allograft rejection.","optionReasons":{"A":"They are the receptors for interleukin-2, which is produced by macrophages when they attack the donor cells. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Donor HLA class II molecules are recognized by recipient CD4 helper T lymphocytes and drive cellular allograft rejection.","B":"Donor HLA class II molecules are recognized by recipient CD4 helper T lymphocytes and drive cellular allograft rejection.","C":"They induce the production of blocking antibodies that protect the graft. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Donor HLA class II molecules are recognized by recipient CD4 helper T lymphocytes and drive cellular allograft rejection.","D":"They induce IgE which mediates graft rejection. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Donor HLA class II molecules are recognized by recipient CD4 helper T lymphocytes and drive cellular allograft rejection."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"6bcf68dc88b8843f220c5b778b06c937d90cca1d8158c834a961114b1e932bea"},"q-380ca96b4cb5":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Hypogastric arteries.","explanation":"The fetal internal iliac (hypogastric) arteries supply the umbilical arteries, which return deoxygenated blood to the placenta.","optionReasons":{"A":"The fetal internal iliac (hypogastric) arteries supply the umbilical arteries, which return deoxygenated blood to the placenta.","B":"Ductus venosus. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The fetal internal iliac (hypogastric) arteries supply the umbilical arteries, which return deoxygenated blood to the placenta.","C":"Portal vein. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The fetal internal iliac (hypogastric) arteries supply the umbilical arteries, which return deoxygenated blood to the placenta.","D":"Inferior vena cava. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The fetal internal iliac (hypogastric) arteries supply the umbilical arteries, which return deoxygenated blood to the placenta.","E":"Foramen ovale. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The fetal internal iliac (hypogastric) arteries supply the umbilical arteries, which return deoxygenated blood to the placenta."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"07140a5ec31e2d033908a7ae72a32d323e6c34a56a48dcb44f9e151fe4349276"},"q-6bb77cae92c6":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Procaine","explanation":"Procaine is an ester anesthetic comparatively hydrophilic and readily formulated as a soluble hydrochloride salt; tetracaine and bupivacaine are more lipophilic.","optionReasons":{"A":"Tetracaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Procaine is an ester anesthetic comparatively hydrophilic and readily formulated as a soluble hydrochloride salt; tetracaine and bupivacaine are more lipophilic.","B":"Etidocaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Procaine is an ester anesthetic comparatively hydrophilic and readily formulated as a soluble hydrochloride salt; tetracaine and bupivacaine are more lipophilic.","C":"Procaine is an ester anesthetic comparatively hydrophilic and readily formulated as a soluble hydrochloride salt; tetracaine and bupivacaine are more lipophilic.","D":"Bupivacaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Procaine is an ester anesthetic comparatively hydrophilic and readily formulated as a soluble hydrochloride salt; tetracaine and bupivacaine are more lipophilic."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"0b10dc7c23c5ecb51690d8bb92d5fc94fd66499cb3cc7645fd3be3b5d2e06f57"},"q-8747a0d3ff54":{"correct":"E","answerText":"They are all forms of non-random sampling","explanation":"Snowball, convenience, quota and purposive approaches are all forms of nonrandom sampling, making 'all of the above' the accurate response.","optionReasons":{"A":"Snowball sampling — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Snowball, convenience, quota and purposive approaches are all forms of nonrandom sampling, making 'all of the above' the accurate response.","B":"Convenience sampling — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Snowball, convenience, quota and purposive approaches are all forms of nonrandom sampling, making 'all of the above' the accurate response.","C":"Quota sampling — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Snowball, convenience, quota and purposive approaches are all forms of nonrandom sampling, making 'all of the above' the accurate response.","D":"Purposive sampling — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Snowball, convenience, quota and purposive approaches are all forms of nonrandom sampling, making 'all of the above' the accurate response.","E":"Snowball, convenience, quota and purposive approaches are all forms of nonrandom sampling, making 'all of the above' the accurate response."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"f59b88211722a6e3659610ee82783ebb18072c2abed1e96a4b6d59b9e8991ab4"},"q-5f23320befe7":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Intermingled delusional and real life orientation","explanation":"Double orientation involves concurrent recognition of actual reality and a delusional interpretation of place or situation.","optionReasons":{"A":"Visual splitting — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Double orientation involves concurrent recognition of actual reality and a delusional interpretation of place or situation.","B":"Oriented to time but not place and person — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Double orientation involves concurrent recognition of actual reality and a delusional interpretation of place or situation.","C":"Having delusional orientation separate from reality — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Double orientation involves concurrent recognition of actual reality and a delusional interpretation of place or situation.","D":"Double orientation involves concurrent recognition of actual reality and a delusional interpretation of place or situation.","E":"None of the above — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Double orientation involves concurrent recognition of actual reality and a delusional interpretation of place or situation."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"28f6c6376e239dff87aafa758f7404c8df139ffa8d02ff4fe00fe0371923759f"},"q-015744083c3c":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Intracellular receptors for lipid soluble ligands","explanation":"Intracellular steroid-hormone receptors may associate with heat-shock proteins in the inactive state until ligand binding changes their conformation.","optionReasons":{"A":"Intracellular steroid-hormone receptors may associate with heat-shock proteins in the inactive state until ligand binding changes their conformation.","B":"Transmembrane receptors Version: 16Oct2008 Page 25 of 42 Pharmacology – Part 1 Quiz — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Intracellular steroid-hormone receptors may associate with heat-shock proteins in the inactive state until ligand binding changes their conformation.","C":"G-protein coupled receptors — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Intracellular steroid-hormone receptors may associate with heat-shock proteins in the inactive state until ligand binding changes their conformation.","D":"Ligand-gated ion channels — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Intracellular steroid-hormone receptors may associate with heat-shock proteins in the inactive state until ligand binding changes their conformation."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"7d46b283019e0893273bcc792cd7632169fa893d8055ac45097cb762abbf977d"},"q-ef9a0c63e524":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Transport against concentration gradient","explanation":"Active transport moves material against an electrochemical gradient using energy directly or indirectly, unlike passive diffusion.","optionReasons":{"A":"Transport of drugs trough a membrane by means of diffusion — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Active transport moves material against an electrochemical gradient using energy directly or indirectly, unlike passive diffusion.","B":"Transport without energy consumption — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Active transport moves material against an electrochemical gradient using energy directly or indirectly, unlike passive diffusion.","C":"Engulf of drug by a cell membrane with a new vesicle formation — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Active transport moves material against an electrochemical gradient using energy directly or indirectly, unlike passive diffusion.","D":"Active transport moves material against an electrochemical gradient using energy directly or indirectly, unlike passive diffusion."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"db106b2a601bf8333268194d3d40c79dd9f4e1205a612f97f448091b5b304427"},"q-bf84d1973515":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Lymph follicles","explanation":"Lymphatic nodules are also called lymph follicles; they are clusters of lymphocytes that may contain germinal centers.","optionReasons":{"A":"Lymphatic nodules are also called lymph follicles; they are clusters of lymphocytes that may contain germinal centers.","B":"White pulp — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lymphatic nodules are also called lymph follicles; they are clusters of lymphocytes that may contain germinal centers.","C":"Peyer's patches — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lymphatic nodules are also called lymph follicles; they are clusters of lymphocytes that may contain germinal centers.","D":"Lymph node — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lymphatic nodules are also called lymph follicles; they are clusters of lymphocytes that may contain germinal centers.","E":"Diffuse lymphatic tissue — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lymphatic nodules are also called lymph follicles; they are clusters of lymphocytes that may contain germinal centers."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"22d4eb43e0af14c8ecfa1d10fdbfb09c84762a89d73169a1e535a579e6dce29b"},"q-916a3e8b3862":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Prevalence ratio","explanation":"The prevalence ratio directly compares prevalences across exposure groups in cross-sectional data, whereas cumulative incidence requires follow-up over time.","optionReasons":{"A":"The prevalence ratio directly compares prevalences across exposure groups in cross-sectional data, whereas cumulative incidence requires follow-up over time.","B":"Prevalence odds ratio — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The prevalence ratio directly compares prevalences across exposure groups in cross-sectional data, whereas cumulative incidence requires follow-up over time.","C":"Cumulative incidence — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The prevalence ratio directly compares prevalences across exposure groups in cross-sectional data, whereas cumulative incidence requires follow-up over time.","D":"None of the above 11 — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: The prevalence ratio directly compares prevalences across exposure groups in cross-sectional data, whereas cumulative incidence requires follow-up over time."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"d00282173b8045e00e2690361eaeeb0f60b9708ce336ccced22721106c6e3151"},"q-9f89faace288":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Oral mifepristone followed by oral miso- prostol (p. 284)","explanation":"A common medication abortion regimen uses oral mifepristone followed by misoprostol by a recommended route; exact regimens vary with gestational age and guideline.","optionReasons":{"A":"Intravenous oxytocin infusion — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A common medication abortion regimen uses oral mifepristone followed by misoprostol by a recommended route; exact regimens vary with gestational age and guideline.","B":"Intramuscular carboprost — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A common medication abortion regimen uses oral mifepristone followed by misoprostol by a recommended route; exact regimens vary with gestational age and guideline.","C":"Intravaginal mifepristone followed by intra- amniotic dinoprost — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: A common medication abortion regimen uses oral mifepristone followed by misoprostol by a recommended route; exact regimens vary with gestational age and guideline.","D":"A common medication abortion regimen uses oral mifepristone followed by misoprostol by a recommended route; exact regimens vary with gestational age and guideline."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"ca5995e3ac2010eb42149e9e339286cc93b6ffb234421a250b881c3b5255b15c"},"q-8e2e85fd8039":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Brain","explanation":"The central nervous system is formed by the brain and spinal cord; cranial and spinal peripheral nerves and ganglia belong to the peripher