oice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: IgM does not significantly cross the placenta, so fetal/neonatal IgM is synthesized by the fetus or neonate rather than transferred from the mother.","C":"It is 50% maternal, 50% fetal in origin. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: IgM does not significantly cross the placenta, so fetal/neonatal IgM is synthesized by the fetus or neonate rather than transferred from the mother.","D":"It is 25% maternal, 75% fetal in origin. — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: IgM does not significantly cross the placenta, so fetal/neonatal IgM is synthesized by the fetus or neonate rather than transferred from the mother.","E":"IgM does not significantly cross the placenta, so fetal/neonatal IgM is synthesized by the fetus or neonate rather than transferred from the mother."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"88a9fffa55ba4fd947f516110fb7be1917ac72553808196c6d90aae2f7d1b34b"},"q-e4b067544d44":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Lidocaine","explanation":"Lidocaine is a local anesthetic and a class Ib antiarrhythmic used to suppress selected ventricular arrhythmias.","optionReasons":{"A":"Cocaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lidocaine is a local anesthetic and a class Ib antiarrhythmic used to suppress selected ventricular arrhythmias.","B":"Lidocaine is a local anesthetic and a class Ib antiarrhythmic used to suppress selected ventricular arrhythmias.","C":"Bupivacaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lidocaine is a local anesthetic and a class Ib antiarrhythmic used to suppress selected ventricular arrhythmias.","D":"Ropivacaine — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Lidocaine is a local anesthetic and a class Ib antiarrhythmic used to suppress selected ventricular arrhythmias."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"73ad5d6a0ba18f4e3ad89af53ccb8e0eeeb1cb9ed0f7913e6bee31abb4ef78bd"},"q-82203a0521e3":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Systematic Sampling","explanation":"Systematic random sampling chooses a random starting position and then selects every kth individual from the ordered sampling frame.","optionReasons":{"A":"Simple Random Sampling — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Systematic random sampling chooses a random starting position and then selects every kth individual from the ordered sampling frame.","B":"Stratified Random Sampling — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Systematic random sampling chooses a random starting position and then selects every kth individual from the ordered sampling frame.","C":"Systematic random sampling chooses a random starting position and then selects every kth individual from the ordered sampling frame.","D":"Cluster sampling — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Systematic random sampling chooses a random starting position and then selects every kth individual from the ordered sampling frame.","E":"Convenience — Not the best choice for the stated question. Distinguishing fact: Systematic random sampling chooses a random starting position and then selects every kth individual from the ordered sampling frame."},"references":[],"review":"independently_reasoned_batch3_provisional_no_original_key","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"efc9ecf53fd1cd32398247ae1fa5e4f6b466adee25ad79f55f0e87d7a2ec0a74"},"q-b3240af98d0c":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Increasing tone of ciliary muscle","explanation":"Pilocarpine causes ciliary muscle contraction, opening trabecular spaces and increasing aqueous outflow through the conventional pathway.","optionReasons":{"A":"Contracting