 recent preceding infection in suspected poststreptococcal glomerulonephritis."},"references":[],"review":"identical_stem_and_options_answer_projection_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"2e754c64cfde42f90877f4c7f050def38050ee7e71571cd909d58060bc8b23a4"},"q-dd7b15fd12b7":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Perikaryon","explanation":"Perikaryon refers to the cell body or soma of a neuron, which contains the nucleus and most synthetic organelles.","optionReasons":{"A":"Ganglion — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Perikaryon refers to the cell body or soma of a neuron, which contains the nucleus and most synthetic organelles.","B":"Perikaryon refers to the cell body or soma of a neuron, which contains the nucleus and most synthetic organelles.","C":"Astrocyte — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Perikaryon refers to the cell body or soma of a neuron, which contains the nucleus and most synthetic organelles.","D":"Nissl — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Perikaryon refers to the cell body or soma of a neuron, which contains the nucleus and most synthetic organelles.","E":"Terminal bouton — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Perikaryon refers to the cell body or soma of a neuron, which contains the nucleus and most synthetic organelles."},"references":[],"review":"identical_stem_and_options_answer_projection_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"ed236088f2806b13c6d0cfe58201612658f96afbfaf11714db8e3fcdcc43f438"},"q-7bc44f3e0960":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Perikaryon","explanation":"Perikaryon refers to the cell body or soma of a neuron, which contains the nucleus and most synthetic organelles.","optionReasons":{"A":"Ganglion — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Perikaryon refers to the cell body or soma of a neuron, which contains the nucleus and most synthetic organelles.","