ed nerve fibers — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Neurofilaments are structural intermediate filaments giving axons mechanical resilience and supporting their caliber.","C":"Cell bodies — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Neurofilaments are structural intermediate filaments giving axons mechanical resilience and supporting their caliber.","D":"Nodes of Ranvier — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Neurofilaments are structural intermediate filaments giving axons mechanical resilience and supporting their caliber.","E":"Neurofilaments are structural intermediate filaments giving axons mechanical resilience and supporting their caliber."},"references":[],"review":"identical_stem_and_options_answer_projection_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"f53f17becf9bc987ba3e1b0b17cb4110a7c39683a2e797413fab210724e00355"},"q-c6e04ac84be2":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Arteriole","explanation":"Arterioles are resistance vessels that regulate blood entry to capillary beds through changes in smooth-muscle tone.","optionReasons":{"A":"Capillary — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Arterioles are resistance vessels that regulate blood entry to capillary beds through changes in smooth-muscle tone.","B":"Arterioles are resistance vessels that regulate blood entry to capillary beds through changes in smooth-muscle tone.","C":"Venule — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Arterioles are resistance vessels that regulate blood entry to capillary beds through changes in smooth-muscle tone.","D":"Elastic artery — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Arterioles are resistance vessels that regulate blood entry to capillary beds through changes in smooth-muscle tone.","E":"Muscular artery — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Arterioles are resistance vessels that regulate blood entry to capillary beds through changes in smooth-muscle tone."},"references":[],"review":"identical_stem_and_options_answer_projection_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"722edb8b8040e1a763fd2e49a14c0760db9724bd5439a7e90ec1db81e0f66ed8"},"q-7a0e4774cafe":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Add an antifungal agent.","explanation":"Persistent fever despite antibacterial treatment in a profoundly neutropenic leukemia patient suggests invasive fungal infection and warrants empiric antifungal coverage in the appropriate high-risk setting.","optionReasons":{"A":"Perform lumbar puncture to assess cerebrospinal fluid. — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Persistent fever despite antibacterial treatment in a profoundly neutropenic leukemia patient suggests invasive fungal infection and warrants empiric antifungal coverage in the appropriate high-risk setting.","B":"Continue present therapy. — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Persistent fever despite antibacterial treatment in a profoundly neutropenic leukemia patient suggests invasive fungal infection and warrants empiric antifungal coverage in the appropriate high-risk setting.","C":"Stop all antibiotics because he likely has drug fever. — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Persistent fever despite antibacterial treatment in a profoundly neutropenic leukemia patient suggests invasive fungal infection and warrants empiric antifungal coverage in the appropriate high-risk setting.","D":"Add an aminoglycoside antibiotic. — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Persistent fever despite antibacterial treatment in a profoundly neutropenic leukemia patient suggests invasive fungal infection and warrants empiric antifungal coverage in the appropriate high-risk setting.","E":"Persistent fever despite antibacterial treatment in a profoundly neutropenic leukemia patient suggests invasive fungal infection and warrants empiric antifungal coverage in the appropriate high-risk setting."},"references":[],"review":"identical_stem_and_options_answer_projection_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"dfd3f16fd2c0d7944f095fc5b6f13141bbd682449279cd5b59a131549790e840"},"q-21a53a94c35e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Lidocaine","explanation":"Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters.","optionReasons":{"A":"Tetracaine — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters.","B":"Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters.","C":"Cocaine — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters.","D":"Procaine 13 — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters."},"references":[],"review":"identical_stem_and_options_answer_projection_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"08a93ce33253237c16158e6f54cc0f0a3d74ae10d537b4009ef5a3624959b70f"},"q-5fd93c12e933":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Lidocaine","explanation":"Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters.","optionReasons":{"A":"Tetracaine — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters.","B":"Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters.","C":"Cocaine — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters.","D":"Procaine 13 — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Lidocaine is an amino-amide local anesthetic of the acetanilide class, whereas procaine, cocaine and tetracaine are esters."},"references":[],"review":"identical_stem_and_options_answer_projection_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"08a93ce33253237c16158e6f54cc0f0a3d74ae10d537b4009ef5a3624959b70f"},"q-a6abc64654f4":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Muscular artery","explanation":"Most named distributing arteries are muscular arteries, which have prominent smooth-muscle media and control regional blood flow.","optionReasons":{"A":"Capillary — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Most named distributing arteries are muscular arteries, which have prominent smooth-muscle media and control regional blood flow.","B":"Arteriole — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Most named distributing arteries are muscular arteries, which have prominent smooth-muscle media and control regional blood flow.","C":"Venule — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Most named distributing arteries are muscular arteries, which have prominent smooth-muscle media and control regional blood flow.","D":"Elastic artery — Alternative not supported by the distinguishing principle: Most named distributing arteries are muscular arteries, which have prominent smooth-muscle media and control regional blood flow.","E":"Most named distributing arteries are muscular arteries, which have prominent smooth-muscle media and control regional blood flow."},"references":[],"review":"identical_stem_and_options_answer_projection_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-19","provisional":true,"questionTextHash":"3b5793e386710c4b4ea18f15e6d0079cdd30578e9e64cdc